{"compound":{"value":"http://bio2rdf.org/cpd:C00101","type":"uri"},"drugDesc":{"value":"Tetrahydrofolic acid is a folic acid derivative. It is produced from dihydrofolic acid by dihydrofolate reductase.\nIt is converted into 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate by serine hydroxymethyltransferase. It is a coenzyme in many reactions, especially in the metabolism of amino acids and nucleic acids. It acts as a donor of a group with one carbon atom. It gets this carbon atom by sequestering formaldehyde produced in other processes.","type":"literal"},"ChemicalEquation":{"value":"C00101 + C00006 <=> C00504 + C00005","type":"literal"},"ReactionTitle":{"value":"Tetrahydrofolate + NADP+ <=> Folate + NADPH","type":"literal"},"drug":{"value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00116","type":"uri"}},
